{
  "schema": "quilt-zip-target/v1",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "CRDT family as Quilt sheet",
    "description": "The CRDT family \u2014 G-Counter, PN-Counter, G-Set, OR-Set, LWW-Register, PN-Vector, RGA \u2014 ported to Quilt. The CRDT merge operation IS the Quilt cell's gossip. The protocol-agnosticism is built into the math, not the implementation. The cross-language bake-off (Fortran, C, Rust, Go, CUDA, PTX) IS the polyformalism demonstration. The CRDT family shows that the protocol doesn't matter \u2014 only the math does.",
    "generated": "2026-08-21T01:52:23Z",
    "address_root": "crdt"
  },
